<title>LATVIA: AVERAGE YIELD ON FIRST TWO-YEAR T-BILL 9.52 PCT.</title>
<headline>AVERAGE YIELD ON FIRST TWO-YEAR T-BILL 9.52 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first two-year Treasury bill auction in Latvia on Wednesday fetched an averaged yield of 9.52 percent with a cupon of 9.50 percent, dealers said.  </p>
<p>All of the 17 million lats issue was sold as it was oversubscribed, with investors placing 48.32 million lats worth of bids, a dealer told Reuters.</p>
<p>The finance ministry is expected to release all of the results from the auction later in the day.</p>
<p>-- Martinsh Gravitis, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
</text>
